{ Original King's Gambit course. Study material, not a historical game. } 1. e4 e5 2. f4 exf4 3. Nf3 Be7 4. Bc4 Bh4+ 5. Kf1 c6 6. Nc3 b5 7. Bb3 a5 8. a3 Be7 9. d4 a4 10. Ba2 d5 { Laboratory starts here. The bishop reaches h4 with check along the diagonal to e1. Kf1 answers it without pushing more kingside pawns, but permanently gives up castling. Develop d4, Nc3 and the queen bishop while finding a safe place for the king. Treat rook coordination as a task; castling is no longer available. } 11. exd5 { Candidate comparison. The pawn captures a pawn on d5. Calculate the best reply before assuming a recapture, then recount material and opened lines. } 11... Nf6 12. dxc6 Ba6 13. Kf2 Nxc6 14. Re1 O-O 15. Bxf4 { Candidate comparison. The bishop captures a pawn on f4. Calculate the best reply before assuming a recapture, then recount material and opened lines. } 15... b4 16. Ne4 bxa3 17. bxa3 Bxa3 18. Bb1 Bb2 19. Rxa4 { Candidate comparison. The rook captures a pawn on a4. Calculate the best reply before assuming a recapture, then recount material and opened lines. } 19... Bb7 20. Rxa8 Bxa8 *

